---
title: The Best Vegan Lasagna
portions: 8
category: Main Course
source: "https://www.lovingitvegan.com/vegan-lasagna/"
---

## Ingredients

### Bolognese
@mushrooms{240g}(cremini)
@tofu{226g}(extra firm, crumbled)
@walnuts{100g}
@onion{1}(medium, chopped)
@garlic{1 Tbsp}(crushed)
@olive-oil{1 Tbsp}
@basil{1 tsp}(dried)
@oregano{1 tsp}
@cayenne-pepper{¼ tsp}
@soy-sauce{1 Tbsp}(dark)
@tomato-paste{½ cup}
@marinara-sauce{1 cup}
@coconut-sugar{1 Tbsp}
salt and pepper to taste

### Cheese Sauce
@olive-oil{6 Tbsp}
@flour{5 Tbsp}
@soy-milk{960 ml}(unsweetened)
@dijon-mustard{2 tsp}
@nutritional yeast{2 tsp}
@onion-powder{½ tsp}
@garlic-powder{1 tsp}
@smoked-paprika{¾ tsp}
salt and pepper to taste

### Assembly
@marinara-sauce{2½ cups}
@lasagna-sheets{12}(spinach)
@zucchini{4}(small, sliced)
fresh basil (chopped)

## Steps

### Bolognese

1. Process mushrooms in a food processor until finely chopped. Transfer to a mixing bowl.
2. Crumble tofu with a fork, add to the bowl.
3. Process walnuts into crumbles, add to the bowl. Mix together.
4. Sauté chopped onions and crushed garlic in olive oil with dried basil, oregano and cayenne until softened.
5. Add the tofu/walnut/mushroom mix, dark soy sauce, tomato paste and marinara sauce. Cook until no visible liquid remains.
6. Season with coconut sugar, salt and pepper.

### Cheese Sauce

7. Heat olive oil in a saucepan until hot.
8. Add flour and fry briefly, stirring vigorously.
9. Add soy milk all at once and whisk vigorously to remove lumps.
10. Bring to the boil stirring constantly. Continue boiling for a few minutes until thickened.
11. Remove from heat and stir in dijon mustard, nutritional yeast, onion powder, garlic powder, smoked paprika, salt and pepper.

### Assemble

12. Preheat oven to 200°C.
13. Add a thin layer of marinara to the bottom of a deep 9×13 dish.
14. Layer: 4 lasagna sheets → half the bolognese → thin layer of cheese sauce → sliced zucchini → all the vegan ricotta.
15. Repeat: 4 lasagna sheets → marinara → thin layer of cheese sauce → remaining bolognese → zucchini.
16. Final layer: 4 lasagna sheets → remaining marinara (save a little for decorating).
17. Cover with foil and bake 30 min.
18. Remove foil, top with remaining cheese sauce, bake uncovered 20 min more.
19. Let rest 5 min, swirl remaining marinara on top, garnish with fresh basil, dried basil and black pepper.
